## Control {{controlId}}: Separate User Functionality from System Management Functionality

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization separates user functionality from system management functionality within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through dedicated administrative accounts, Privileged Identity Management (PIM), and role-based access control enforced by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if directoryRolesConfigured}}
**Role-Based Separation:**
{{directoryRolesCount}} directory roles define the boundary between user and administrative functionality. Administrative actions require assignment to specific roles with separate privileged accounts distinct from standard user accounts.
{{else}}
Directory role configuration has not been confirmed. Role-based separation between user and administrative functions is not verified.
{{/if}}

{{#if pimConfigured}}
**Privileged Identity Management:**
Azure AD PIM enforces just-in-time (JIT) elevation for administrative access. Administrators use standard user accounts for daily operations and activate privileged roles only when performing system management tasks, with time-bound activation and approval workflows.
{{else}}
Privileged Identity Management has not been configured. Administrative access separation relies on static role assignments without JIT elevation.
{{/if}}

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Administrative Access Enforcement:**
Conditional Access policies enforce additional controls for administrative sessions:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/each}}
{{else}}
Conditional Access enforcement for administrative sessions has not been configured.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Azure AD directory role assignments, PIM activation logs, administrative account separation documentation, and Conditional Access policies targeting admin roles.

